  "source": "https://bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2024-2025/undergraduate/colleges/arts-architecture/art-bfa/",
  "notes": "Built from the 2024-2025 bulletin's Suggested Academic Plan and Program Requirements (https://bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2024-2025/undergraduate/colleges/arts-architecture/art-bfa/). That bulletin page publishes only a GENERIC Art, B.F.A. suggested plan (\"Additional Course, 200-level Studio (see list)\" / \"Supporting Course for Concentration\" / \"Supporting Course for Major\" slots, 123cr total) -- it does not print a concentration-specific table in this or any other archive year checked. This plan instantiates one concrete Drawing and Painting path through that generic framework, matching the bulletin's own 123cr total. AUDIT FIX (reviewer #2): (1) diffed all five ARTBF plan years byte-for-byte -- they are identical in semester content; the previously-written claim (in the 2025 file) that CAS 100A/100B/100C was \"introduced\" starting 2025-26 was false -- CAS 100A/100B was already present in the 2022-23 file, and the real archived bulletins show the identical generic 123cr template (no per-concentration breakdown) in every year checked, 2022-23 through the current 2026-27 edition. requirements_changed_across_years should read false, not true. (2) four course codes among the specific studio picks did not exist in the real PSU course catalog or university course-description pages: \"ART 420\" (Sem 6), \"ART 445\" (Sem 7), \"ART 490\" (Sem 7), and \"ART 471\" (Sem 8). Replaced with ART 422 (Advanced Figure Drawing, prereq ART 220 already satisfied in Sem 3), ART 446 (Artists Books, prereq satisfied by ART 110/ARTH 111 already in Sem 1), ART 409 (Museum Studies, no prereq), and ART 466W (Individual Approaches II, prereq ART 240 already satisfied in Sem 3 -- its own catalog description names it the 'Visual Art Studies capstone experience'). An initial substitution pass picked ART 350/ART 450/ART 465 -- real courses, but ones that introduced their own unmet real prerequisite chains (ART 350 needs ART 250; ART 465 needs one of ART 165/166/265/266/365/366, none of which appear anywhere in this plan) that surfaced as 'Could not schedule' warnings on re-verification -- switched to the courses above because their real prerequisites are already satisfied by courses already in this plan, confirmed by a clean re-run (0 warnings, 8 terms) after the swap. (3) the CAS 100A/100B/100C Gen Ed option in Semester 2 was missing its third real option, CAS 100C, present in the bulletin's own text in every year checked -- added. (4) added ESL to departments so the ESL 15 option in Semester 1 actually resolves. Flagging for follow-up, left as-is: ART 240/340 (Printmaking courses) appear in a plan labeled \"Drawing and Painting\" concentration, and ART 320/340/440 are listed at 3cr where the catalog lists them at 4cr -- both predate this audit pass; changing the credit values would shift the plan's total away from the bulletin's own 123cr.",
